:: Church encounter - power confession [bg-guesthouse]
<h1 class="ptitle">GUEST HOUSE</h1>
<br /><br />
/* A nun of the power path hears a guest's confession and blesses the sin instead of forgiving it. The player can listen, and help them act on it. */
<<set _ce = setup.churchEncounters>>
<<set _fx = setup.nurseryEncounters>>
<<set _cast = _ce.cast()>>
<<if !_cast>>
	<<goto 'Guest house'>>
<<else>>
<<set _nun = _cast.nun, _guest = _cast.guest, _partner = _cast.partner ?? null>>
<<set _nunName = setup.displayName(_nun), _gName = setup.displayName(_guest)>>
<<set _nHe = setup.pronounceWhat(_nun), _nHis = setup.pronounceWhos(_nun), _nHim = setup.pronounceWho(_nun)>>
<<set _gHe = setup.pronounceWhat(_guest), _gHis = setup.pronounceWhos(_guest), _gHim = setup.pronounceWho(_guest)>>
<<set _gMc = setup.npc.mcName(_guest), _nMc = setup.npc.mcName(_nun)>>
/* Widget arguments can't start with [, which SugarCube reads as link markup */
<<set _justGuest = [_guest], _guestAndNun = [_guest, _nun]>>

Someone has hung a blanket across the corner by the stove to make a little booth of it. From behind it comes the low murmur of a voice, and every so often a soft, breathy sound that is definitely <<=_nunName>>.
<br /><br />
<<sayNpc _nun>>
	Go on. Don't stop there. Tell me all of it.
<</sayNpc>>
<br />
Through the gap at the edge of the blanket you can see <<=_gName>> on <<=_gHis>> knees, and <<=_nunName>> sitting over <<=_gHim>> with <<=_nHis>> hands folded very properly in <<=_nHis>> lap and <<=_nHis>> cheeks very improperly pink.
<br /><br />

<div id="ce_choices">
	<<link 'Listen in'>>
		<<replace '#ce_choices'>>
			<<addmins 15>>
			<<run _ce.byNun(_nun, _guest, 'corruption', 1, 2)>>
			<<run _ce.byNun(_nun, _nun, 'corruption', 1, 2)>>
			You stay where you are, very still.
			<br /><br />
			<<if _partner>>
				<<set _pName = setup.displayName(_partner), _pHe = setup.pronounceWhat(_partner), _pHis = setup.pronounceWhos(_partner), _pHim = setup.pronounceWho(_partner)>>
				<<sayNpc _guest>>
					It was <<=_pName>>. We were both on the late watch, and it was so cold, and <<=_pHe>> said we should share the blanket. And then <<=_pHis>> hand was on my thigh, and I didn't move it. I put mine on top of it and pushed it higher. We did it right there against the wall of the woodshed, with the fire going out, and I didn't care who heard.
				<</sayNpc>>
				<br />
				<<=_nunName>> says nothing, only leans a little closer, lips parted. <<=_gName>>'s voice drops lower.
				<br /><br />
				<<sayNpc _guest>>
					And the worst part is I keep thinking about it. At meals. While I'm working. I look at <<=_pHim>> across the room and I want <<=_pHim>> again. If <<=_gMc>> ever found out, I'd die.
				<</sayNpc>>
			<<else>>
				<<sayNpc _guest>>
					It was in the garden. I was picking for supper, and there was this zucchini. It was enormous, and smooth, and still warm from the sun. And I just... I took it back to my bunk. I didn't even cook it. I wasn't thinking about cooking.
				<</sayNpc>>
				<br />
				There is a long pause from behind the blanket. <<=_nunName>> makes a small, strangled sound that might be a cough. <<=_gName>> plows on.
				<br /><br />
				<<sayNpc _guest>>
					And then I put it back in the basket for supper. Everyone ate it. You ate it. <<=ucfirst(_gMc)>> had seconds.
				<</sayNpc>>
			<</if>>
			<br />
			<<=_nunName>> takes a slow, unsteady breath. When <<=_nHe>> speaks, <<=_nHis>> voice is warm and low.
			<br /><br />
			<<sayNpc _nun>>
				Listen to me. There's nothing here that needs forgiving. You say you sinned. I hear that you <em>felt</em>. You hungered and you let yourself be fed. The divine made that hunger in you, and it's holy. Go and give thanks for it. Every time. And don't fear <<=_nMc>>. Of everyone in this house, <<=_nMc>> would understand best of all.
			<</sayNpc>>
			<br />
			<<=_gName>> looks up at <<=_nHim>> as if <<=_gHe>> can't quite believe what <<=_gHe>> is hearing. Neither of them seems to have noticed how close they are now, or how quickly they are both breathing.
			<br /><br />
			<<set _likesNun = _ce.pairOk(_guest, _nun, _nun)>>
			<<set _nunScene = _likesNun ? _ce.guestScene([_guest, _nun]) : null>>
			<<set _wantsMc = _ce.mcOk(_guest)>>
			<<set _trio = _ce.threesome(_guest, _nun)>>
			<<set _blocked = _ce.mcBlockedBy()>>
			/* The nun goes along with a partner she isn't drawn to for the sake of her faith, at a little cost to her will */
			<<set _yieldGuest = _ce.nunYields(_nun, [_guest]) ? _ce.byNunChanges(_nun, [{ npc: _nun, stat: 'sub', low: 1, high: 2 }]) : []>>
			<<set _nunGain = _ce.byNunChanges(_nun, [{ npc: _nun, stat: 'corruption', low: 1, high: 2 }])>>
			<<set _soloGains = [{ npc: _guest, stat: 'corruption', low: 3, high: 5 }].concat(_nunGain)>>
			<<set _joinGains = _ce.byNunChanges(_nun, [{ npc: _guest, stat: 'corruption', low: 4, high: 6 }]).concat(_nunGain)>>
			<div id="ce_options">
				<<if _nunScene>>
					<<link `'Encourage ' + _nHim + ' to show ' + _nHis + ' devotion'`>>
						<<run _joinGains.concat(_yieldGuest).forEach(c => _fx.change(c.npc, c.stat, c.low, c.high))>>
						<<replace '#ce_options'>>
							You clear your throat softly. They both jump. <<=_nunName>> sees you through the gap in the blanket, and instead of pulling away, <<=_nHe>> smiles.
							<br /><br />
							<<you>>
								Don't stop on my account. Show <<=_gHim>> what you mean.
							<</you>>
							<br />
							<<=_nunName>> cups <<=_gName>>'s face in both hands and kisses <<=_gHim>>, slow and deep, and <<=_gName>> melts into it with a little moan of relief. A moment later they are on their feet and stumbling toward the dormitory, already tugging at each other's clothes.
							<br /><br />
							<div id="ce_after">
								<<ceWatchLinks _nunScene _guestAndNun>>
								<<nurseryEffects>>
							</div>
						<</replace>>
					<</link>>
					<<linkdesc>><<=_ce.changesText(_joinGains.concat(_yieldGuest))>><</linkdesc>>
					<<if _wantsMc && _trio>>
						<<if _blocked>>
							<div class="link-internal" style="background: #ccc">Join them (<<=_blocked>>)</div>
						<<else>>
							<<link 'Step behind the blanket and join them'>>
								<<replace '#ce_options'>>
									You draw the blanket aside and step into the little booth. <<=_gName>> starts, and for a heartbeat looks ready to bolt, caught on <<=_gHis>> knees with <<=_gHis>> confession still hanging in the air. But <<=_nunName>> only smiles up at you, unsurprised, as if <<=_nHe>> had been expecting you all along.
									<br /><br />
									<<sayNpc _nun>>
										You see? The divine hears every confession. And sometimes it sends an answer.
									<</sayNpc>>
									<br />
									<<=ucfirst(_nHe)>> takes <<=_gName>>'s hand and guides it up to rest against you. <<=_gName>> looks from <<=_nHim>> to you, breathing unsteadily, and then the last of the hesitation goes out of <<=_gHim>>.
									<br /><br />
									<<sayNpc _guest>>
										Please, <<=_gMc>>. Don't make me wait any longer.
									<</sayNpc>>
									<br />
									<<ceSexLink 'Continue' 'threesome' _trio _joinGains.concat(_yieldGuest)>>
									<<nurseryEffects>>
								<</replace>>
							<</link>>
						<</if>>
					<</if>>
				<<elseif _wantsMc>>
					<<set _soloLabel = 'Invite ' + _gHim + ' to work out that excitement with you'>>
					<<if _blocked>>
						<div class="link-internal" style="background: #ccc"><<=_soloLabel>> (<<=_blocked>>)</div>
						<<if _trio>><div class="link-internal" style="background: #ccc">Invite <<=_nunName>> to join you both (<<=_blocked>>)</div><</if>>
					<<else>>
						<<ceSexLink _soloLabel 'solo' _justGuest _soloGains>>
						<<if _trio>>
							<<set _trioLabel = 'Invite ' + _nunName + ' to join you both'>>
							<<ceSexLink _trioLabel 'threesome' _trio _joinGains.concat(_yieldGuest)>>
						<</if>>
					<</if>>
				<</if>>
				[[Leave them to their prayers|Guest house]]
				<<nurseryEffects>>
			</div>
		<</replace>>
	<</link>>
	[[Leave them to their confession|Guest house]]
</div>
<</if>>
